%% Pending text edit request state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no pending text tap" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No pending tap candidate exists.
    There is no document mutation, selection change,
    preview state, repaint request, or action event.
  end note

  Idle --> Disposed: "runtime.dispose()"
  Idle --> FirstTapGate: "finite tap or click admitted"
  Idle --> Idle: "invalid, stale, drag, active pointer conflict, or wrong mode / ignore"

  state "First tap gate" as FirstTapGate
  note right of FirstTapGate
    First tap detection is gesture tracking only.
    It reads current hit data and may remember a text
    candidate, but it never edits committed document state.
  end note

  FirstTapGate --> TopHitFirst: "query committed content hit candidates"
  FirstTapGate --> Idle: "non-finite world position or tapSlop exceeded / no request"

  state "Top visible selectable hit first" as TopHitFirst
  note right of TopHitFirst
    Spatial and geometry policy choose the first exact
    visible selectable content element in paint order.
    Background and non-selectable content cannot qualify.
  end note

  TopHitFirst --> Idle: "no top hit / no request"
  TopHitFirst --> Idle: "top hit is not text / no request"
  TopHitFirst --> PendingCandidate: "top hit is text / store id, generation, elementRevision, positions, timestamp, epoch"

  state "Pending text tap candidate" as PendingCandidate
  note right of PendingCandidate
    Pending state is input history only:
    element id, generation, elementRevision, view/world positions,
    timestamp, and controllerEpoch.
    It is not CanvasPreviewState and not Store state.
  end note

  PendingCandidate --> SecondTapGate: "second tap or explicit double-tap"
  PendingCandidate --> CleanupOnly: "delay exceeded, slop exceeded, invalid sample, no hit, mode mismatch, controllerEpoch mismatch, mode change, or interactive=false"
  PendingCandidate --> CleanupOnly: "loadDocument success after install"
  PendingCandidate --> PendingCandidate: "loadDocument validation/materialization failure before install / preserve tap; no emit, repaint, or mutation"
  PendingCandidate --> DisposeCleanup: "runtime.dispose()"

  state "Second tap gate" as SecondTapGate
  note right of SecondTapGate
    The second tap must be revalidated against the
    current committed document and current epoch.
  end note

  SecondTapGate --> CleanupOnly: "non-finite world position, tapSlop exceeded, doubleTapSlop exceeded, or delay exceeded"
  SecondTapGate --> TopHitSecond: "query current committed content hit candidates"

  state "Second top-hit gate" as TopHitSecond
  note right of TopHitSecond
    The current top visible selectable content hit wins
    before checking element kind. A text element behind
    a non-text top hit cannot request editing.
  end note

  TopHitSecond --> CleanupOnly: "no top hit / clear pending only"
  TopHitSecond --> CleanupOnly: "top hit is not text / clear pending only"
  TopHitSecond --> CandidateMatch: "top hit is text"

  state "Candidate match gate" as CandidateMatch
  note right of CandidateMatch
    The second text hit must match the pending element
    and still be visible, selectable, text, generation-current,
    elementRevision-current, and epoch-current.
  end note

  CandidateMatch --> CleanupOnly: "different text, stale generation, stale elementRevision, hidden, unselectable, or epoch mismatch"
  CandidateMatch --> EmitRequest: "same current text element"

  state "Issue guarded app-owned text edit request" as EmitRequest
  note right of EmitRequest
    InteractionEngine issues CanvasInteractionRequestId
    through InteractionRequestRegistry, then emits
    CanvasTextEditRequested with request id, element id,
    controllerEpoch, documentRevision, elementRevision,
    timestamp, view/world positions, boundsWorld, and
    immutable text snapshot. documentRevision is observation-only.
    This is not an EditKernel commit and not a document/action mutation.
  end note

  EmitRequest --> IssuedRequestLive: "request delivered / clear pending tap and keep request id live"

  state "Issued request remains live" as IssuedRequestLive
  note right of IssuedRequestLive
    The application owns Flutter editor overlay, IME,
    focus, accessibility, hide/show policy, and later
    commitTextEdit text commit flow outside this request state.
    Pending tap history is already cleared.
    The registry is not an active text-input session and
    not CanvasPreviewState.
  end note

  IssuedRequestLive --> RetiredRequest: "commitTextEdit accepted no-op or changed text / retire request"
  IssuedRequestLive --> RetiredRequest: "commitTextEdit stale rejection / retire known stale request"
  IssuedRequestLive --> RetiredRequest: "loadDocument success / controllerEpoch makes request stale"
  IssuedRequestLive --> Disposed: "runtime.dispose() / later commitTextEdit throws StateError"

  state "Retired or stale request id" as RetiredRequest
  note right of RetiredRequest
    Retired and epoch-stale request ids cannot commit.
    Stale rejection uses request id, controllerEpoch,
    generation, elementRevision, missing element, and
    current text-family mismatch; documentRevision is not
    a stale guard, so unrelated document edits do not reject.
  end note

  RetiredRequest --> Idle: "request lifecycle closed"

  state "Cleanup only" as CleanupOnly
  note left of CleanupOnly
    Cleanup clears pending tap history only.
    It publishes no text request, action event,
    document revision, selection change, preview update,
    spatial update, projection eviction, or repaint.
  end note

  CleanupOnly --> Idle: "pending candidate cleared"
  DisposeCleanup --> Disposed: "clear pending tap and close textEditRequests stream"

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  Disposed --> Disposed: "later mutating operation or pointer sample / StateError"
  Disposed --> Disposed: "dispose again / no side effects"

  note left of PendingCandidate
    Negative invariants:
    no selected-move resolver;
    no main-scene or overlay preview;
    no direct DocumentStoreKernel mutation;
    no EditKernel commit;
    no legacy architecture as normative source.
  end note
